# Implementation Plan - WBCSD Protocol Upgrade

The goal is to strictly adhere to the WBCSD Cement Industry Protocol for CO2 calculation. This involves expanding the data models to cover all relevant scopes (1 & 2) and providing a calculation-centric UI.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This upgrade changes the simple data entry workflow to a more comprehensive protocol-based calculator.

## Proposed Changes

### Backend (`emissions`)

#### [MODIFY] [models.py](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/cement/backend/emissions/models.py)
*   **FuelConsumption**: Add `biomass_percentage` (Decimal, default 0). Calculate `biogenic_co2` separately from `fossil_co2`.
*   **ClinkerProduction**: Add `non_carbonate_mgo_contribution` (Decimal, default 0).
*   **[NEW] ElectricityConsumption**:
    *   Fields: `facility`, `period`, `grid_emission_factor` (kg CO2/kWh), `kwh_consumed`.
    *   Calculates: `scope_2_co2`.
*   **[NEW] RawMaterialConsumption**:
    *   Method B for Calcination.
    *   Fields: `material_name`, `quantity`, `carbonate_content_%`, `moisture_%`.

